20260527.113422.935 [<kpop..........] [So the issue is:]
20260527.113423.103 [<kpop..........] [1. Static faiss is built on Linux via faiss-sys with CMAKE_TOOLCHAIN_FILE pointing to openblas.]
20260527.113425.666 [<kpop..........] [2.]
20260527.113425.765 [<kpop..........] [The static Faiss build uses OpenBLAS via CMAKE_TOOLCHAIN_FILE but ends up linking only libblas.so.3 and liblapack.so.3]
20260527.113426.055 [<kpop..........] [instead of libcblas or OpenBLAS libraries. Since cblas_dgemm exists in libcblas.so.3 but isn't linked, the runtime requires]
20260527.113426.281 [<kpop..........] [cblas linkage. The fix involves modifying `emit_blas_lapack_link_search_linux` or `enn_py_build` to include libcblas or]
20260527.113426.396 [<kpop..........] [OpenBLAS during Python extension building. Additionally, the enn-py build process only invokes]
20260527.113427.644 [<kpop..........] [`emit_linux_rpath_link_args()` and skips both `emit_faiss_link_search` and `emit_blas_lapack_link_search_linux`.]
20260527.113427.735 [<kpop..........] [The ennbo build process calls `emit_faiss_link_search()` on Linux, which falls through to]
20260527.113428.119 [<kpop..........] [`emit_blas_lapack_link_search_linux()` when `faiss_c` is not found. Since there's no FAISS_LIB_DIR and no `libfaiss_c` in]
20260527.113428.216 [<kpop..........] [conda, the system searches for `faiss_c` in standard paths. If not found, it invokes `emit_blas_lapack_link_search_linux()`.]
20260527.113428.729 [<kpop..........] [However, the build should link OpenBLAS, and `openblas_for_link` should detect `libopenblas.so.0` in conda to emit the]
20260527.113429.727 [<kpop..........] [correct link argument.]
20260527.113429.959 [<kpop..........] [The static Faiss build embeds BLAS, but the Python extension's ndarray-linalg still requires cblas linkage at link time. The]
20260527.113430.017 [<kpop..........] [built .so file references libblas.so.3, yet cblas symbols remain undefined, indicating missing cblas linking.]
20260527.113430.254 [<kpop..........] [The fix involves updating `emit_blas_lapack_link_search_linux` to also link libcblas when OpenBLAS isn't used, or to prefer]
20260527.113430.453 [<kpop..........] [OpenBLAS over separate BLAS/cblas libraries.]
20260527.113430.503 [<kpop..........] [The `openblas_for_link` function does find libopenblas.so.0 in conda lib, so the issue likely stems from CONDA_PREFIX not]
20260527.113431.171 [<kpop..........] [being set during build, preventing proper detection and linking of OpenBLAS.]
20260527.113431.328 [<kpop..........] [The static Faiss build uses OpenBLAS via CMAKE_TOOLCHAIN_FILE, but the final .so file links libblas.so.3 instead of]
20260527.113431.530 [<kpop..........] [OpenBLAS. The hypothesis is that faiss-sys correctly uses OpenBLAS during static build, but ndarray-linalg separately links]
20260527.113434.733 [<kpop..........] [BLAS through Rust's link attributes, causing a mismatch.]
20260527.113434.917 [<kpop..........] [The ndarray-linalg crate may be linking `-lblas -llapack` without cblas, which could cause missing cblas symbol errors.]
20260527.113434.957 [<kpop..........] [Possible fixes include:]
20260527.113435.126 [<kpop..........] [1. Adding `cargo:rustc-link-lib=cblas` in `emit_blas_lapack` when libcblas exists but split libs are used]
20260527.113435.291 [<kpop..........] [2. Explicitly linking OpenBLAS in `emit_openblas_link` and ensuring it's called for enn-py builds]
20260527.113435.452 [<kpop..........] [3. Rebuilding with `maturin develop` after applying the fix]
20260527.113435.813 [<kpop..........] [Additionally, the enn-py build does not invoke `emit_faiss_link_search`it only handles rpath. Therefore, blas linking for]
20260527.113436.111 [<kpop..........] [the cdylib originates from ennbo's build.rs, which is the build script for the ennbo crate that enn-py depends on.]
20260527.113436.395 [<kpop..........] [When enn-py links ennbo as an rlib, the ennbo crates build script runs and should execute]
20260527.113436.674 [<kpop..........] [`emit_blas_lapack_link_search_linux`. This function checks for `CONDA_PREFIX` and calls `emit_openblas_link` if OpenBLAS is]
20260527.113436.882 [<kpop..........] [found. However, since `CONDA_PREFIX` isn't set during the build, `emit_openblas_link` is never invoked, leading to incorrect]
20260527.113439.528 [<kpop..........] [linking of BLAS instead of OpenBLAS.]
20260527.113439.708 [<kpop..........] [If `openblas_for_link` finds OpenBLAS, it prints the full path to the .so file using `cargo:rustc-link-arg`, which should]
20260527.113439.865 [<kpop..........] [link OpenBLAS directly. However, if ndarray-linalg adds `-lblas` or if link order is incorrect, it might override the]
20260527.113440.000 [<kpop..........] [OpenBLAS linking. Alternatively, the extension might have been built without `CONDA_PREFIX` set. Rebuilding with]
20260527.113441.027 [<kpop..........] [`CONDA_PREFIX` properly set may resolve the issue; otherwise, a code fix to explicitly link `libcblas` will be needed.]
20260527.113441.198 [<kpop..........] [The user can temporarily work around the issue by setting `LD_PRELOAD` to point to `libcblas.so` when running tests.]
20260527.113441.393 [<kpop..........] [However, a permanent solution requires updating the build process to properly link `libcblas`. Specifically,]
20260527.113441.543 [<kpop..........] [`emit_blas_lapack_link_search_linux` should include `libcblas` in its linking logic when cblas symbols are required.]
20260527.113441.735 [<kpop..........] [Alternatively, the fix could be implemented in `faiss_blas_toolchain` for static Faiss builds or in `link_search.rs` by]
20260527.113442.155 [<kpop..........] [adding a function to detect and link `libcblas` explicitly. The goal is to ensure that when cblas symbols are needed, the]
